[TEXT] **Root cause found.** Router6's iptables **FORWARD chain** has an ACL on `iifname "eth2"` (the r6_r3 link from router3) that:
1. Allows only TCP/80 from 172.16.10.0/24 → 172.18.51.1
2. **Drops all TCP** (any src/dst)
3. **Drops all UDP** — 75 packets already dropped
4. **Drops all other protocols (ICMP etc.)** — 38 packets already dropped

This blocks all transit traffic from the entire rest of the network into the 172.18.51.x subnet through router6. Router6's own pings work (host-originated, not FORWARDED); pc15–pc18 reach each other locally (L2 via mswitch2, not through router6's FORWARD chain). The fault matches the `acl-skill` family — direct evidence confirmed on router6, Phase 5 proceeds.

